# Try Head Office from Visual Studio or VS Code (REST Client): click "Send Request" above each block.
# 1. Start the API (http profile). 2. Set @adminKey to your user-secrets admin key.
# 3. Run the requests in order, pasting the ids/code/key from each answer into the variables.

@host = http://localhost:5180
@adminKey = paste-your-admin-key-here
@tenantId = paste-tenant-id
@storeId = paste-store-id
@apiKey = paste-api-key

### Is it running?
GET {{host}}/health

### 1. Create a business (tenant)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/tenants
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nep Liquor" }

### 2. Create its store (the code must match the register's StoreId, e.g. STORE-001)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/tenants/{{tenantId}}/stores
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "storeCode": "STORE-001", "name": "Parramatta" }

### 3. Make a one-time activation code for that store
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/stores/{{storeId}}/activation-codes
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "validDays": 7 }

### 4. Activate a register with the code (what the register will do in step 3)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "paste-the-code", "registerCode": "REG-001", "deviceName": "Front counter" }

### 5. Send an event (copy a row from the register's OutboxMessages table to test with real data)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/sync/events
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "events": [
    {
      "eventId": "5f0c2a8e-6a3e-4c1b-9a51-2d1c7e0b9f41",
      "type": "journal.recorded",
      "version": 1,
      "storeId": "STORE-001",
      "registerId": "REG-001",
      "sequence": 1,
      "occurredAtUtc": "2026-11-14T09:12:44Z",
      "payload": { "eventType": "SignIn", "detail": "Owner signed in" }
    }
  ]
}

### 6. Heartbeat
POST {{host}}/api/v1/heartbeat
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### 7. Registers at the store (shows last seen)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/stores/{{storeId}}/registers
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
